<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bureau of Insular Affairs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1939</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bureau of Insular Affairs was an agency of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> War <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> that oversaw the civil government of territories acquired after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish-American War</a>, chiefly the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> and, for a time, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>. Created in 1898 and given its name in 1902, it was dissolved in 1939, its work passing to the Interior Department.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bureau-of-insular-affairs.jpg" alt="Bureau of Insular Affairs" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:US-BureauOfInsularAffairs-Insignia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
